  "case": "SM 2.2 rule 9's agent app: T3 Code's server, t3 serve, runs Claude Code for the app's clients, so the session's nearest non-shell ancestor is the server, parent_class agent_app (SM 1.2). On Linux T3's background service runs it from systemd's user manager; on macOS from launchd, as a LaunchAgent; on Windows it was typed into PowerShell in Windows Terminal and runs through T3's npm launcher, a node that starts the t3 executable. The walk stops at t3 in each, so neither the terminal above it nor the scheduler decides.",
  "source": "Written by hand from SM 1.2 and 2.2 rule 9 and from T3 Code's source at d8f3feff (scripts/npm-launcher/t3.mjs starts <T3 home>/runtime/versions/<version>/t3; apps/server/src/serviceLauncher.ts and cloud/bootService.ts write the systemd unit and the launchd plist), not recorded on a machine. T3 starts claude with node's child_process, so claude stays in t3's process group, with no terminal.",
